.TH GO 1
.SH NAME
go \- build, test, install, and manage Go modules and programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B go
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B go
command is the primary interface to the Go toolchain. It builds and tests
packages, manages modules and workspaces, installs commands, formats packages,
and invokes lower-level tools.
.PP
Run
.B go help
for the current command list,
.BI "go help " command
for command-specific documentation, and
.B go env
for the effective toolchain environment.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Compile packages and dependencies.
.TP
.B test
Compile and test packages.
.TP
.B install
Compile and install packages and commands.
.TP
.B mod
Manage modules and their dependencies.
.TP
.B work
Manage multi-module workspaces.
.TP
.B tool
Run a named Go tool.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The command is configured by variables including
.BR GOENV ,
.BR GOFLAGS ,
.BR GOPATH ,
.BR GOPROXY ,
.BR GOROOT ,
.BR GOOS ,
and
.BR GOARCH .
Use
.B go env
for authoritative descriptions and current values.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gofmt (1)
.PP
The complete version-matched documentation is available through
.B go help
and in the Go source package.
